	(uuid "3d47e3ea-60d5-41c5-b021-a5e3af8316b2")
	(paper "A4")
	(lib_symbols)
	(text "Phasing network design for UHF Canted Turnstile Antenna + L1 GPS Patch Antenna \n\n437.5 MHz - UHF \n\n1.57542 GHz- GPS L1 \n\n3 QBA-07+ Power splitters for phasing network (Oresat0 used the same ones for their tri-band turnstile) \n\n4 UHF antenna elements with target relative phases of 0°, 90°, 180°, and 270° (Clockwise)\n\n50 ohm RF transmission lines using GCPW \n\nLC impedance matching on UHF antenna ports 2 and 4 (20 nH, 7.1 pF) \n\nPort 2 and 4 have simulated impedances that require impedance matching, we used LC matching \n\n6-layer PCB using JLCPCB's JLC06161H-3313 stack up \n\nMMCX connector to UHF Ebyte carrier board; separate SMA connector for gps antenna \n\nUSB-C PD input for external power during testing/charging \n\nMOSFET-controlled burn-wire circuit for antenna deployment \n\n "
